v0.1.0 — a pure-P2P, Taproot-only Bitcoin wallet for iOS

The first release. Winnow (then btc-swift) speaks the Bitcoin P2P protocol
directly — no backend, no indexer, no API keys. BIP157/158 compact filters
drive the read side; the wallet is BIP86 Taproot-only by construction.

This release stood up the whole spine: the wire protocol and framing, header
sync with proof-of-work checking, compact-filter matching, coin selection and
PSBTv2 signing, transaction relay with mempool visibility, and an end-to-end
UI test suite driving a real build against a custom signet — seven scenarios,
with the screenshots that became the public site. CI runs the package suite,
the app suite, and the signet e2e on self-hosted macOS runners, with a
resume-once guard that ended the first flaky-CI crash.
